Journey: Broker submission <scenarioId> appears in the customer's My claims grid
Id: broker-claim-in-grid
Tags: @portal @api @grid @data-driven @integration @regression
Risk: 4
Requirements: API-2, PORTAL-7
Description: Seed through the partner API, verify in the UI. Rows come from the broker's JSON feed: first batch only (JSONPath), broker channel only, runFlag Yes.

Set variable incidentDate to format(addDays(today(), -number("<daysAgo>")), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Set variable externalRef to unique("HB-")
Call API "POST ${API_URL}/v1/claims" with body '{"policyId":"<policyId>","type":"<type>","incidentDate":"${incidentDate}","amountClaimed":<amount>,"description":"<description>","externalRef":"${externalRef}"}' as broker and store as created
Expect the created response status is 201
Expect response created matches schema "schemas/claim.schema.json"
Capture "$.claimId" from created as claimId
Expect response created "$.channel" equals "BROKER"
Expect response created "$.externalRef" equals "${externalRef}"

# The policyholder the row names signs in (the role is test data too)
Log in as <role>
Click the "My claims" link
  Expect the page contains "claims"
Type "${claimId}" into the "Search claims" field
  Expect the page contains "1 claim"
Expect the My claims grid to have a row where Claim is "${claimId}"
Expect the Status of the row where Claim is "${claimId}" in the My claims grid to be "Submitted"
Expect the Amount of the row where Claim is "${claimId}" in the My claims grid to be "<amount>"
Expect the Type of the row where Claim is "${claimId}" in the My claims grid to be "<type>"
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#removeClaim" with claimId="${claimId}" as cleanup

Examples: from data "data/partner-submissions.json" path "$.batches[0].submissions" where channel = BROKER and runFlag = Yes
